# Control, not ownership, decides (CR 614.1a, 108.4): "a creature an opponent controls". Bot1 casts Vren on turn 1, and on turn 3 gives its own
# Ornithopter to Bot2 with Harmless Offering. Bot2 now controls it, so when Bot1 bolts it Vren exiles it instead of letting it die - it is not
# put into Bot1's (its owner's) graveyard - and it was exiled under an opponent's control, so the end step makes one Rat, 2/2 beside Vren.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Vren, the Relentless
Ornithopter
Harmless Offering
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vren, the Relentless.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Ornithopter
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Harmless Offering
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Toughness = 2
